
v0.5.0:
 - BUG FIX: a `.GZ` ASN database is decompressed, CSV lines are trimmed, and a prefix with host bits set is still loaded
 - BUG FIX: a country code that is not two letters is rejected instead of panicking
 - BUG FIX: a large Linux journald record can be sealed and sent
 - BUG FIX: a log format failure is reported instead of panicking, and syslog is sent before the reconnect wait
 - BUG FIX: a non-ASCII size string in worker or statsd config is rejected instead of panicking
 - BUG FIX: a quit during graceful shutdown closes the unique control listener
 - BUG FIX: a relative pid file is created in the working directory from before daemonizing, and the lock is held until the process exits
 - BUG FIX: a statsd export continues after `sendmmsg` writes only part of the batch, and logs the first error in each 64 second slice
 - BUG FIX: a timestamp offset that includes seconds is written in UTC
 - BUG FIX: a UDP listen `scale` whose denominator is 0 is rejected instead of panicking
 - BUG FIX: after graceful shutdown is cancelled, a later SIGTERM still requests shutdown
 - BUG FIX: an empty daemon group uses `_.sock` as the control socket
 - BUG FIX: an IP location lookup returns an error if the query runtime has quit, instead of panicking
 - BUG FIX: continent and country counts include the last code
 - BUG FIX: failure to spawn the async log thread is reported
 - BUG FIX: IPv4 and IPv6 reuseport listeners use separate eBPF maps, so `0.0.0.0` and `::` no longer share one
 - BUG FIX: on Windows, another control client can connect while one connection is still open
 - BUG FIX: the Windows hostname sent to syslog no longer includes a trailing NUL
 - Feature: a valid lookup that matches neither database increments `server.lookup_not_found`
 - Feature: the packaged build includes the eBPF UDP reuseport selector used for a lossless upgrade. Root attaches it unless `use_ebpf` is false
 - Feature: `vey-iploc-get` looks up one or more addresses over a UDP or Unix datagram socket
 - Feature: `vey-iploc-ctl query <ip>` looks up one address in the running databases
 - Feature: `vey-iploc-ctl reload` re-reads `server` and `geoip_db`, restarts changed listeners, and swaps the running databases
 - Breaking: listen sockets are `server` entries. UDP uses one reuseport socket per worker when `worker` is set, and one socket on the main runtime otherwise. Unix datagram listen is supported. `UDP_LISTEN_ADDR` and `-G port<port>` no longer select the listen address. `-G` still names the instance and its control socket
 - Breaking: the default control socket directory is `/run/vey-iploc` for root on Linux and `/var/run/vey-iploc` for root on other Unix systems; another Linux user uses an absolute `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` or `/run/user/<uid>/vey-iploc`
 - Compatibility: a reuseport listener does not join eBPF maps pinned by a previous release
 - Compatibility: bump MSRV to 1.94.0
 - Compatibility: DragonFly worker `sched_affinity` applies to the calling thread
 - Compatibility: published container images set OCI labels so GHCR can describe them

v0.4.0:
 - Feature: optional jemalloc or mimalloc global allocator at compile time; allocator name/version appear in `--version`
 - Feature: derive default config / log / metrics / controller names from the binary name (supports renamed installs)
 - Compatibility: bump MSRV to 1.91.0

v0.3.1:
 - BUG FIX: fix build of deb package

v0.3.0:
 - Compatibility: bump MSRV to 1.86.0
 - Deprecated: the following config options are deprecated:
     - emit_duration in statsd config, use emit_interval instead

v0.2.0:
 - Feature: listen to Ctrl-C event and shutdown gracefully
 - Feature: allow to run in multiple worker threads

v0.1.0:
 - Initial release
